  "finalStateTail": " accents, a segmented gradient progress line, and a live telemetry counter.\\n\\nAll code was written by the three delegated tools — I only coordinated: ChatGPT desktop supplied the design concept, Codex CLI proposed the carousel treatment and interaction spec, and Claude Code in the Git Bash window wrote the actual files (index.html, styles.css, app.js) in the project folder alongside the design brief. I never wrote or edited any code file myself.\\n\\nVerification in the browser: the page loads with all five slides (Aurora Field Notes, Ink Studies, Signal Garden, Night Atlas, Echo Archive). Keyboard works — arrows orbit, Home/End jump to first/last, and a real Enter keypress activates the focused card (deck jumped 05→04 with the manifesto expansion starting and the lime focus ring visible in the screenshot). Clicking a side card navigates the deck directly. Auto-advance was observed live (deck moved on its own about every 4.6 seconds, pausing under the pointer and when the tab is hidden). The developer console is clean, and the \\\"00 — ORBIT INDEX\\\" label is an intentional ornament. One nuance: synthetic Enter events injected by test tooling don't trigger button activation — that was a tool limitation, confirmed not a site bug by the real-keypress test.\"}}],\"results\":[{\"id\":\"call_33012a5be737488db75cd773\",\"content\":\"{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"summary\\\":\\\"The homepage is built and verified. Aurora Atelier is a stylized nocturnal design-practice homepage with a special orbit carousel in the header: five tilted cards riding a dashed orbit rail, a coral-lit front card, lime accents, a segmented gradient progress line, and a live telemetry counter.\\\\n\\\\nAll code was written by the three delegated tools — I only coordinated: ChatGPT desktop supplied the design concept, Codex CLI proposed the carousel treatment and interaction spec, and Claude Code in the Git Bash window wrote the actual files (index.html, styles.css, app.js) in the project folder alongside the design brief. I never wrote or edited any code file myself.\\\\n\\\\nVerification in the browser: the page loads with all five slides (Aurora Field Notes, Ink Studies, Signal Garden, Night Atlas, Echo Archive). Keyboard works — arrows orbit, Home/End jump to first/last, and a real Enter keypress activates the focused card (deck jumped 05→04 with the manifesto expansion starting and the lime focus ring visible in the screenshot). Clicking a side card navigates the deck directly. Auto-advance was observed live (deck moved on its own about every 4.6 seconds, pausing under the pointer and when the tab is hidden). The developer console is clean, and the \\\\\\\"00 — ORBIT INDEX\\\\\\\" label is an intentional ornament. One nuance: synthetic Enter events injected by test tooling don't trigger button activation — that was a tool limitation, confirmed not a site bug by the real-keypress test.\\\",\\\"success\\\":true,\\\"verified\\\":true,\\\"final\\\":true}\"}],\"metadata\":{}}],\"seenMessages\":[\"1790135096184\"],\"compactions\":13},\"attachments\":[]}"
